["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/bic", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Business Identifier Code (BIC), also known as SWIFT-BIC or SWIFT code, is a unique 8 or 11-character alphanumeric code standardized by [ISO 9362](https://www.iso.org/standard/84108.html) to identify financial and non-financial institutions (e.g., `BBWCUS33`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N736591ee7cb84bbabe130a2070860cf3", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/contactType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ContactPointRelationshipType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isni", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI)](https://isni.org/page/what-is-isni/) is a unique identifier used to distinguish the public identities of parties involved in the creation, production, and distribution of media content. Standardized by [ISO 27729](https://www.iso.org/standard/87177.html), it consists of 16 characters\u201415 digits plus a final check character\u2014and is often represented as a URI, such as `https://isni.org/isni/000000012146438X`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nee0d0ccd0c334a2b82007f458c0b243f", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N83c5dcbc126d4de285365c3bc1396844", "localId", "", ""]
